    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d151">

                <pb facs="0293" n="263" sameAs="frus:frus1872p2v5/pg263"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">No. 12.</note>
                <head>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 379.]</seg>
                    <lb/> Mr. Bancroft to Mr. Fish.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-06-28"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi>
                            28, 1872</date>. (Received July 15.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am officially informed that the names of
                    the gentlemen who will be requested to examine and report upon the Haro boundary
                    question will be forwarded to the Imperial Arbitrator to-day for his approval.
                    This approval will follow as a matter of course, and if the gentlemen designated
                    accept the appointment, the consideration of the case will go forward without
                    delay. I am assured that everything which is proper will be done to accelerate a
                        decision.<seg type="margin">Appointment of gentlemen to examine Haro
                        boundary question.</seg></p>
                <p>I remain, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GEO. BANCROFT.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
